<h2 id="price">When it's cheapest</h2>
<p>Prices follow demand from the US and Canada. The most expensive weeks are Christmas to New Year, Presidents' Day weekend, spring break in March and Easter. The cheapest periods are <b>late August to early November</b> (minus the Mexican national holiday around 16 September) and the two or three weeks after Easter. A good compromise for value and weather is the <b>first half of December</b> or <b>late April to mid-May</b> on the Pacific.</p>

<h2 id="holidays">Dates that fill up</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Semana Santa (Holy Week)</b>, in March or April, is Mexico's biggest domestic holiday. Beaches near big cities get very busy.</li>
<li><b>Day of the Dead</b>, 31 October to 2 November, fills hotels in Oaxaca, Mexico City, Mérida and the colonial towns.</li>
<li><b>Guelaguetza</b> in July and the <b>Cervantino</b> in October book out Oaxaca and Guanajuato.</li>
<li><b>Spring equinox</b> around 20-21 March draws large crowds to Chichén Itzá.</li>
</ul>
